

README — Hamiltonian‑Astrophysical Genetics Simulation Engine (H‑AGSE)

Author: C. Matthew BlackwellVersion: 1.0Document Type: Scientific System Overview

Overview

The Hamiltonian‑Astrophysical Genetics Simulation Engine (H‑AGSE) is a unified computational architecture designed to model astrophysical structures, genetic regulatory networks, and molecular dynamics using a single Hamiltonian energy formulation. The system integrates multi‑scale datasets, enforces strict encryption standards, and executes high‑performance simulations across 33 orders of magnitude of physical scale.

This README provides a concise introduction to the system’s purpose, mathematical foundation, architecture, and usage domains.

Purpose

H‑AGSE addresses fragmentation in scientific modeling by applying one governing energy‑minimization principle across multiple scientific domains. The engine enables researchers to analyze:

Astrophysical structures

Genetic regulatory networks

Molecular dynamics

under a unified Hamiltonian framework.

Mathematical Foundation

The system is governed by two Hamiltonian expressions:

[ H = -J \sum \sigma_i \sigma_j - h \sum \sigma_i ]

[ H = -J \sum \alpha_i \sigma_i - h \sum \sigma_i ]

Key components:

σᵢ — Spin variables

J — Coupling constant

h — External field

αᵢ — Domain weighting

These variables are mapped to astrophysical, genetic, and molecular domains.

System Architecture

Input Layer

Accepts astrophysics datasets, genetic/molecular datasets, and Hamiltonian blueprint parameters.

Encryption Layer

Implements AES‑256, FIPS 140‑2 compliance, and HSM‑based key management.

H‑Core Engine

Includes Hamiltonian solver, Ising model mapping, perturbation analysis, and multi‑domain state translation.

Computation Layer

Runs simulation modules for:

Gene regulatory networks

Protein folding

Cellular dynamics

Cosmic‑web formation

on cloud and HPC infrastructure.

Visualization Layer

Provides 3D rendering of energy landscapes and domain‑specific structures.

Security Layer

Enforces role‑based access control, audit logging, TLS 1.3, and double‑encryption pathways.

Cross‑Scale Capability

H‑AGSE applies the same Hamiltonian across:

Molecular scale (~10⁻⁹ m)

Genetic/cellular scale (~10⁻⁶–10⁻⁵ m)

Mesoscopic scale (~10⁻³–10⁻¹ m)

Cosmic scale (~10²⁴ m)

This represents 33 orders of magnitude of physical reality.

